---A single geo-blocking rule on a merchant. Multiple rules of the same scope
---are OR-combined: any matching rule blocks the request. When both DENY and
---ALLOW rules are configured, DENY rules are evaluated first — a matching
---DENY blocks the request even if the user is on a separate ALLOW list.
---
---`listMode` controls interpretation (defaults to `DENY`):
---- `DENY`: the listed countries/states are blocked.
---- `ALLOW`: ONLY the listed countries/states are permitted; everything else
---  is blocked.
---
---A rule may specify `countries` (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes), `states`
---(US state codes), or both.
---
---- `scope: GLOBAL` applies to BOTH withdrawal and checkout flows; only valid
---  with `method: IP` (the only method that makes sense for both flows).
---- `method: KYC_ADDRESS` is only valid with `scope: WITHDRAWAL`.
---- `method: BILLING_ADDRESS` is only valid with `scope: CHECKOUT`.
---- `method: IP` is **strictly** fail-closed in both DENY and ALLOW modes:
---  missing IP, failed lookup, or an unresolvable US state resolved from
---  the IP rejects the withdrawal. Both the resolved country and the
---  resolved state (US-only) are evaluated on every request against the
---  rule's `countries` and `states` lists. Skipped on merchant-initiated
---  payouts where no end-user IP exists (`merchantInitiated: true`).
---- `method: GEOLOCATION` is a **best-effort, optional** signal and only
---  valid with `scope: WITHDRAWAL`. When the caller supplies a fresh,
---  resolvable `userLocation`, the rule enforces strictly against the
---  block list. When the signal is absent (browser permission denied,
---  merchant did not send coords, stale capture, or reverse-geocode
---  failure), enforcement is skipped — pair with an `IP` rule for hard
---  real-time enforcement.
---@class coinflow.customers.IBlockingRule
